{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier","kind":"proposition","title":"The Wedderburn--Artin mass sum is the inverse non-commutative Fourier transform on $H_n(q)$","cites":["references/jones1987","references/kassel1995","references/fulton1997"],"tags":["wedderburn-artin","peter-weyl","non-commutative-fourier","hecke-algebra","plancherel"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.WedderburnFourier.peter_weyl_decomposition","text":"wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.md","leanSource":"wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier\"></a><p><strong>Statement.</strong>\n<em>The character expansion driving the three-invariant mass formula operates identically to the inverse non-commutative Fourier transform on the semisimple Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code>.</em></p>\n<p>The mechanism and its role in the mass formula are described in\n<a href=\"#rem:wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier-context\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mutant-jones-bloch-group\">the non-commutative-Fourier reading</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.17.8","page":"b/prop-wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.WedderburnFourier.peter_weyl_decomposition","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
